{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DTX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0002": "$s, t : R \\to U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} = [U/R]$", "MATH_0004": "$|R| \\to |U| \\times |U|$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0006": "$|U|$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-points-presentation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:59e39a5f8cd507b6c7ee4cbe691940a2142ed70fd7fac3f50fbc1cf9c3c493c6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e230804df657ff9a7a69d7387f034bcfd9e9451ef11e8cc16ea3d30ee7720808", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a groupoid in algebraic spaces such that\n<MATH_0002> are flat and locally of finite presentation.\nConsider the algebraic stack <MATH_0003> (see above).\nThen the image of <MATH_0004> is an equivalence relation\nand <MATH_0005> is the quotient of <MATH_0006> by this equivalence relation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:63c200ede9d7219a5450c533ba65d7c8d75558f3760cf8d7c141986143549e2d", "unit_id": "tag:0DTZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DTX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$|U| \\to |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$R = U \\times_\\mathcal{X} U$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n|R| \\longrightarrow |U| \\times_{|\\mathcal{X}|} |U|\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$|R| \\to |U| \\times |U|$", "MATH_0006": "$(u_1, u_2) \\in |U| \\times |U|$", "MATH_0007": "$u_1$", "MATH_0008": "$u_2$", "MATH_0009": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{criteria-lemma-flat-quotient-flat-presentation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-characterize-surjective}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-groupoids-lemma-quotient-stack-2-cartesian}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-points-cartesian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b0e3db85c8802a8753219c0657bc99abb1f2328b3c1c6786182f963a9e1359e0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b43573010183f007267b2b5734354f9fd5b373f8136fbd098a0a09f1128a7549", "source_text": "The induced morphism <MATH_0001> is surjective, flat,\nand locally of finite presentation, see\nCriteria for Representability, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nHence <MATH_0002> is surjective by\nProperties of Stacks, Lemma\n<REF_0002>.\nNote that <MATH_0003>, see\nGroupoids in Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nHence\nProperties of Stacks, Lemma <REF_0004>\nimplies the map\n<MATH_0004>\nis surjective. Hence the image of <MATH_0005> is\nexactly the set of pairs <MATH_0006>\nsuch that <MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008> have the same image in <MATH_0009>.\nCombining these two statements we get the result of the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b4a9f0d4dc9b7c9cb128c96e07fd3fc8c78ab00b13fa0db77a164260de2f2a64", "unit_id": "tag:0DTZ:proof"}
